      "target": {
        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix: handle detached gateway spawn errors",
        "body": "Fixes #101458\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where update respawn could crash the current Node process when a detached gateway child emitted an asynchronous spawn error.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nDetached update handoff now attaches an `error` listener to the spawned child before calling `unref()`. The listener intentionally keeps the handoff non-blocking while preventing Node from treating the child error event as an unhandled exception in the parent.\n\n## User Impact\n\nOperators running update respawn paths no longer risk losing the active gateway process because an asynchronous detached child spawn failure was emitted without a listener.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Added focused coverage in `src/infra/process-respawn.test.ts` for registering the child `error` listener before `unref()`.\n- `git diff --check`\n- Attempted: `node scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/infra/process-respawn.test.ts`, blocked locally because this sparse checkout has no `node_modules`; the runner reported `OPENCLAW_MISSING_VITEST` and requested `pnpm install --frozen-lockfile`.\n",
        "branch": "fix/detached-gateway-spawn-error-101458",
